[{"label":"Movable type on the web","html":"<article class=\"paper\" data-variant=\"classic\" aria-labelledby=\"p2-title\">\n  <header class=\"paper-hero\">\n    <p class=\"paper-venue\"\n      ><span>Journal of Web Typography · Vol. 1 · <time datetime=\"2026-10\">October 2026</time></span></p\n    >\n    <h1 class=\"paper-title\" id=\"p2-title\"\n      >Movable Type on the Web<span class=\"paper-title-sub\">The compositor's rules as stylesheet properties</span></h1\n    >\n    <ul class=\"paper-authors\"\n      ><li>Aron Homberg</li\n      ><li>Claude</li></ul\n    >\n  </header>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-abstract\" aria-labelledby=\"p2-abstract\">\n    <h2 id=\"p2-abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n    <p\n      >Book typography set its text by rules a compositor applied by hand: justified columns, hyphenation, an indent\n      instead of a blank line, an initial at the opening, small capitals for its first line, ligatures and old-style\n      figures. Each rule now has a CSS property. We collect them in one typesetting block and show that a two-column\n      page set with them reads like print on a wide screen and like a book page on a phone.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <nav class=\"paper-toc\" aria-labelledby=\"p2-toc\">\n    <h2 id=\"p2-toc\">Contents</h2>\n    <ol>\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#p2-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1&nbsp;</span>The column</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#p2-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2&nbsp;</span>The paragraph</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#p2-s3\"><span class=\"paper-num\">3&nbsp;</span>The letter</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#p2-cite\"><span class=\"paper-num\">·&nbsp;</span>Citation and references</a></li\n      >\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n\n  <div\n    class=\"typeset typeset-numbered paper-wide\"\n    lang=\"en\"\n    data-columns=\"2\"\n    data-rule\n    data-align=\"justify\"\n    data-indent\n    data-initial=\"drop\"\n    data-lead=\"smallcaps\"\n    data-ligatures=\"classic\"\n  >\n    <h2 class=\"h3 typeset-span\" id=\"p2-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1</span> The column</h2>\n    <p\n      >A printed column is a measure of even grey. The compositor justified each line by adding space between words and,\n      where the space grew too wide, broke a word at a syllable. On the web the same work is done by text-align: justify\n      and hyphens: auto, provided the block names its language; the browser then hyphenates by the rules of that\n      language and keeps the last line of each paragraph flush to the start.</p\n    >\n    <p\n      >Two columns halve the measure and keep the line within the sixty to seventy characters a reader takes in at a\n      glance. The column property takes a count and a minimum width; when the page grows too narrow for two columns of\n      that width, the block sets one, and the phone reads a single column without a separate layout.</p\n    >\n    <h2 class=\"h3 typeset-span\" id=\"p2-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2</span> The paragraph</h2>\n    <p\n      >A book separates its paragraphs by an indent of one em, not by a blank line: the column stays whole, and the eye\n      finds a new thought by its first line alone. The first paragraph after a heading starts flush - the heading has\n      already opened it. The initial-letter property sinks the first letter of the opening paragraph three lines deep,\n      and the first line follows in small capitals.</p\n    >\n    <figure class=\"paper-table typeset-span\">\n      <table class=\"table\">\n        <thead\n          ><tr><th scope=\"col\">Rule</th><th scope=\"col\">Property</th></tr></thead\n        >\n        <tbody>\n          <tr\n            ><td>Blocksatz</td><td><code>text-align: justify</code>, <code>hyphens: auto</code></td></tr\n          >\n          <tr\n            ><td>Einzug</td><td><code>text-indent: 1em</code> on following paragraphs</td></tr\n          >\n          <tr\n            ><td>Initiale</td><td><code>initial-letter: 3</code></td></tr\n          >\n          <tr\n            ><td>Kapitälchen</td><td><code>font-variant-caps: all-small-caps</code></td></tr\n          >\n          <tr\n            ><td>Ligatures, old-style figures</td\n            ><td><code>font-variant-ligatures</code>, <code>font-variant-numeric</code></td></tr\n          >\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <figcaption class=\"typeset-caption\" data-align=\"center\"\n        >Each rule is one data attribute of the typeset block.</figcaption\n      >\n    </figure>\n    <div class=\"separator typeset-span\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-line=\"none\">⁂</div>\n    <h2 class=\"h3 typeset-span\" id=\"p2-s3\"><span class=\"paper-num\">3</span> The letter</h2>\n    <p\n      >Ligatures such as fi, fl and ffi, discretionary ones such as ct and st, and old-style figures that sit in the\n      line like lowercase letters - 1450, 1469, 2026 - render where the font carries them; a font without the features\n      sets the plain forms and loses nothing else.</p\n    >\n    <figure class=\"typeset-group typeset-span\">\n      <figure>\n        <div\n          class=\"chart\"\n          style=\"height: 8rem\"\n          role=\"img\"\n          aria-label=\"Bar chart: lines per page in this paper's two settings - one column 38, two columns 76\"\n          data-chart='{\"grid\":{\"left\":32,\"right\":8,\"top\":12,\"bottom\":24},\"xAxis\":{\"type\":\"category\",\"data\":[\"One column\",\"Two columns\"]},\"yAxis\":{\"type\":\"value\"},\"series\":[{\"type\":\"bar\",\"data\":[38,76],\"label\":{\"show\":true,\"position\":\"top\"}}]}'\n        ></div>\n        <figcaption class=\"typeset-subcaption\">Lines per page, illustrative.</figcaption>\n      </figure>\n      <figure>\n        <img src=\"images/mk-wide.png\" alt=\"A placeholder scene, neutral grey\" />\n        <figcaption class=\"typeset-subcaption\">A picture spanning its cell.</figcaption>\n      </figure>\n      <figure>\n        <table class=\"table\"\n          ><tbody\n            ><tr><td>Measure</td><td>60-70 ch</td></tr\n            ><tr><td>Leading</td><td>1.65</td></tr\n            ><tr><td>Indent</td><td>1 em</td></tr></tbody\n          ></table\n        >\n        <figcaption class=\"typeset-subcaption\">The setting in numbers.</figcaption>\n      </figure>\n      <figcaption class=\"typeset-caption\" data-align=\"justify\"\n        >A chart, a picture and a table in one dense box across both columns; each part lettered, the whole numbered\n        with the paper's figures.</figcaption\n      >\n    </figure>\n  </div>\n  <section class=\"paper-bibtex\" aria-labelledby=\"p2-cite\">\n    <h2 id=\"p2-cite\">Citation and references</h2>\n    <figure class=\"bibtex\" data-formats=\"bibtex apa mla ieee\" aria-label=\"Cite this paper\">\n      <figcaption>Cite this paper</figcaption>\n      <pre><code class=\"bibtex-source\">@techreport{homberg2026movabletype,\n  title = {Movable Type on the Web: The Compositor's Rules as Stylesheet Properties},\n  author = {Homberg, Aron and Claude},\n  institution = {defuss},\n  year = {2026},\n  month = oct,\n  url = {https://shadcn.defuss.org/papers/paper-two-column.html}\n}</code></pre>\n    </figure>\n    <figure class=\"bibtex\" data-formats=\"ieee apa bibtex\" data-format=\"ieee\" aria-label=\"References\">\n      <figcaption>References</figcaption>\n      <pre><code class=\"bibtex-source\">@book{bringhurst2004elements,\n  author = {Bringhurst, Robert},\n  title = {The Elements of Typographic Style},\n  edition = {3},\n  publisher = {Hartley \\& Marks},\n  address = {Vancouver},\n  year = {2004}\n}\n\n@book{tschichold1928typographie,\n  author = {Tschichold, Jan},\n  title = {Die neue Typographie},\n  publisher = {Verlag des Bildungsverbandes der Deutschen Buchdrucker},\n  address = {Berlin},\n  year = {1928}\n}\n\n@misc{w3c-css-inline-3,\n  author = {{W3C}},\n  title = {CSS Inline Layout Module Level 3},\n  howpublished = {W3C Working Draft},\n  url = {https://www.w3.org/TR/css-inline-3/}\n}\n\n@misc{homberg2026defussshadcn,\n  author = {Homberg, Aron},\n  title = {defuss-shadcn: shadcn-style components as semantic HTML},\n  year = {2026},\n  howpublished = {GitHub},\n  url = {https://github.com/kyr0/defuss-shadcn}\n}</code></pre>\n    </figure>\n  </section>\n</article>\n","individual":false}]
